<title>SOUTH KOREA: Fire hits Algerian-registered ship off S.Korea.</title>
<headline>Fire hits Algerian-registered ship off S.Korea.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Algerian-registered cargo vessel, carrying 488 tonnes of car tyres, caught fire off South Korea on Thursday, a fire department official at the port of Pusan said.</p>
<p>No casulties were reported.</p>
<p>The vessel, 14,290-gross ton Babor, with 33 Algerian crew members aboard, was heading for Saudi Arabia after leaving the South Korea port of Pohang, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The fire has been brought under control although we can still see some smoke from the ship,&quot; the official said.</p>
</text>
